        "subject": "accountancy",
        "chapter": "Admission of Partner",
        "body": "On the admission of a new partner, X and Y are the old partners, sharing profits in their old ratio of 3:2. The only revaluation changes are an increase in an asset of ₹40,000, a decrease in an asset of ₹5,000, a decrease in a liability of ₹10,000 and an increase in a liability of ₹5,000. What are X’s and Y’s respective shares of the net revaluation gain?",
        "options": [
          "X: ₹24,000; Y: ₹16,000",
          "X: ₹12,000; Y: ₹8,000",
          "X: ₹27,000; Y: ₹18,000",
          "X: ₹20,000; Y: ₹20,000"
        ],
        "correct_answer": "A",
        "explanation": "An increase in an asset and a decrease in a liability are gains; a decrease in an asset and an increase in a liability are losses. The net revaluation gain is ₹40,000 + ₹10,000 − ₹5,000 − ₹5,000 = ₹40,000. Sharing this gain in the old ratio of 3:2 gives X ₹24,000 and Y ₹16,000.",
