        "id": "ac07a2c4-84ad-4e0d-ae94-3a35007ed2a0",
        "subject": "accountancy",
        "chapter": "Share Capital",
        "body": "A company forfeited 100 shares of ₹10 each, issued at par and fully called up. At the time of initial issue, ₹4 per share had been received and ₹6 per share remained unpaid. All 100 shares are now being reissued as fully paid. No other forfeited shares or amounts are included. What is the maximum aggregate discount permitted on reissue?",
        "options": [
          "(A) ₹400",
          "(B) ₹1,000",
          "(C) ₹600",
          "(D) ₹0"
        ],
        "correct_answer": "A",
        "explanation": "The discount allowed on reissue cannot exceed the amount received on the forfeited shares at their initial issue. The maximum aggregate discount is therefore 100 × ₹4 = ₹400.",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "route": "numerical",
        "family_id": "pyq:cuet2024-accountancy-bookA-q17",
